official data
The catch
USA Today headlined the release “September jobs report shows slowdown in hiring, unemployment ticks up”.
24
In the establishment survey, an over-the-month employment change of about 122,000 is statistically significant, and the household survey's threshold is about 650,000.
1
29,000 is far under that bar, so the survey cannot tell September's change from no change at all.
1
The household count of people employed rose by 406,000 from August.
1
The rise in the number of people employed is under the household survey's bar of about 650,000.
1
More people were working in September, and the labor force grew by more than employment did (485,000 against 406,000).
1
The count of unemployed rose by 78,000 and the rate moved from 4.1 to 4.2 percent.
1
Unrounded, a St. Louis Fed note dated Oct. 2, 2026,
16
says the rate “increased slightly from 4.141% to 4.175%”, so most of the visible tenth is rounding.
