record
On the current payroll series, the twelve monthly changes through August average 45,250 jobs. 4 of the last twelve months were declines. The nine months of 2026 average 68,000 jobs. The series prints 159044 for September and 159015 for August.
9
Table B-1 counts employees on nonfarm payrolls in thousands and prints 159,015 and 159,044. The difference of 29 in that table is the release's change of 29,000.
1
computed
How those averages were counted
Each month is that month's payroll total minus the month before, from the series saved October 3. The twelve months before September, September 2025 through August 2026, sum to 543 thousand and divide by 12 to 45,250. The release states that average as 45,000. The last twelve months include four declines: October 2025, December 2025, February 2026, and July 2026. The 2026 average is January through September, 612 thousand divided by 9.
CNBC reported that economists surveyed by Dow Jones had looked for job growth of 84,000 and an unemployment rate of 4.1 percent. Reuters, writing before the release, said its survey of economists expected 90,000 jobs and a 4.1 percent rate for a third month. Estimates ranged from as low as 35,000 to as high as 180,000. CBS reported a FactSet forecast of 90,000. The Associated Press said economists had expected about 90,000.
